# 🔥 Queue — C++ vs Java vs Python

Queue follows **FIFO — First In, First Out**.

```text
FRONT                         BACK
  ↓                             ↓
[10] [20] [30] [40]
 ↑                              ↑
remove                         add
```

The first element added is the first one removed.

---

## 1. Creating a Queue

| Language         | Syntax                                   |
| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| **C++**          | `queue<int> q;`                          |
| **Java**         | `Queue<Integer> q = new ArrayDeque<>();` |
| **Python list**  | `q = []`                                 |
| **Python deque** | `q = deque()`                            |
| **Python Queue** | `q = Queue()`                            |

### Recommended

```text
C++     → queue
Java    → ArrayDeque
Python  → collections.deque
```

For normal single-threaded queue problems, `collections.deque` is usually the convenient Python choice.

