# 🔥 Python Queue Comparison

Python actually gives you **three common ways** to make a queue.

| Feature       | `list`      | `collections.deque` | `queue.Queue`     |
| ------------- | ----------- | ------------------- | ----------------- |
| Add           | `append()`  | `append()`          | `put()`           |
| Remove        | `pop(0)`    | `popleft()`         | `get()`           |
| Front         | `[0]`       | `[0]`               | No direct access  |
| Back          | `[-1]`      | `[-1]`              | No direct access  |
| Size          | `len()`     | `len()`             | `qsize()`         |
| Empty         | `not q`     | `not q`             | `empty()`         |
| Front removal | O(n)        | O(1)                | O(1)              |
| Main use      | Simple list | Fast queue          | Thread-safe queue |

### ⭐ For DSA practice:

```text
Python → collections.deque
```

is generally the best choice for a normal queue.

